  "body": "MAINLINE-028b complete on 019’s fixed 411.299 kg reserve, with stock-envelope panels and geometry-dependent 028 joining. Two adjustable factors suffice in each commissioned case: gamma and wrinkling; no singleton works. AF’s fixed 0.015 film remains original O5 at full, so it is not erased from the optimism accounting.\n\nSR-200 uses 1850 kg/m³, 290 GPa and the explicit 345 MPa tensile-as-compression assumption. The exact 021b nu=0.33 comparison is preserved; the sheet-based scalar nu=0.0752 check is reported separately. Enforcing 028’s assumed 10 MPa scarf-shear screen gives maximum remaining usages 0.971978 nominal, 0.996076 primer and 0.651469 laboratory bond/ideal weld. Physical joining at the resized points is 215.742, 227.880 and 50.151 kg. Only excess above the existing joint allowance is charged; the laboratory case retains its unused allowance. All factors, subsets, six continuum modes and seam screens are tabulated.\n\nThe nominal/primer six-mode optima alone fail the scarf screen. After enforcing it, full-endpoint reoptimized SF is only 1.006358/1.002803. Bond, peel, weld/HAZ and other local modes remain unqualified; installed-hull SF is unknown.\n\nThe 255 MPa sensitivity has no floating set: even a zero-core face-only upper bound is SF=0.958217. Optimized full-endpoint SFs are 0.869846/0.866848/0.870902.\n\nTwelve checks passed; 16 upstream pins verified; 22 NFI rows. No successor is named. Awaiting the next queued job.",
